hadiths[24]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21426","Al-Walid ibn Muslim and Muhammad ibn Musab al-Qarqasani narrated to us, al-Walid saying: al-Awzai narrated to me, and Muhammad saying: al-Awzai narrated to us, that al-Zuhri narrated to him from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah from Ibn Abbas that he disputed, he and al-Hurr ibn Qays ibn Hisn al-Fazari, concerning the companion of Musa, peace be upon him, whose meeting he sought the way to, so Ibn Abbas said: He is Khadir, when Ubayy ibn Kab passed by them, so Ibn Abbas called him and said: I disputed, I and this companion of mine, concerning the companion of Musa, peace be upon him, whose meeting he sought the way to, so did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mention his affair. He said: Yes, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: While Musa, peace be upon him, was among a company of Bani Israil, a man stood to him and said: Do you know anyone more knowledgeable than you. He said: No. So Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed to him: Our servant Khadir. So Musa, peace be upon him, asked the way to meet him, and Allah, Blessed and Exalted, made the fish a sign for him, so it was said to him: When you lose the fish, return, for you shall meet him. Ibn Musab said in his hadith: So he stopped at a stop and Musa, peace be upon him, said to his youth: Bring us our morning meal, we have indeed met from this journey of ours fatigue. At that he lost the fish, so they returned upon their tracks retracing, and Musa, peace be upon him, began following the trace of the fish in the sea. He said: Of their affair was what Allah, Blessed and Exalted, narrated in His Book."
"21427","Muhammad ibn Bishr al-Abdi narrated to us: Misar narrated to us from Musab ibn Shaybah from Abu Habib ibn Yala ibn Umayyah from Ibn Abbas who said: A man came to Umar and said: The hyenas have eaten us, Misar meaning: the year of drought. So Umar asked him from whom he was, and kept tracing his lineage until he knew him, and he was Musa. So Umar said: If a man had a valley or two valleys he would seek a third to them. So Ibn Abbas said: No belly of the son of Adam is filled except by dust, then Allah turns to whoever repents. So Umar said to Ibn Abbas: From whom did you hear this. He said: From Ubayy. He said: When morning comes, come to me in the morning. So he returned to Umm al-Fadl and mentioned that to her, and she said: What is it with you and speaking with Umar, and Ibn Abbas feared Ubayy had forgotten, so his mother said: Ubayy perhaps did not forget. So he went in the morning to Umar, with him the stick, and we set out to Ubayy, and Ubayy came out to them having performed ablution and said: Madhi afflicted me so I washed my private part, or my opening, Misar doubted. So Umar said: Does that suffice. He said: Yes. He said: Did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Yes. And he asked him about what Ibn Abbas said, and he confirmed him."
"21428","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani from Yazid ibn al-Asamm from Ibn Abbas who said: A man came to Umar asking him, and he began looking at his head once and at his feet another, whether he saw upon him any wretchedness, then Umar said to him: How much is your wealth. He said: Forty camels. Ibn Abbas said: So I said: Allah and His Messenger spoke truth: If the son of Adam had two valleys of gold he would seek a third, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah turns to whoever repents. So Umar said: What is this. I said: Thus Ubayy taught it to me. He said: Then take us to him. He said: So he came to Ubayy and said: What does this one say. Ubayy said: Thus the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught it to me. He said: Should I affirm it. So he affirmed it."
"21429","Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik and Affan narrated to us, both saying: Abu Awanah narrated to us from al-Aswad ibn Qays, Affan saying in his hadith: al-Aswad ibn Qays narrated to us, from Nubayh from Ibn Abbas that Ubayy said to Umar: O Commander of the Believers, I received the Quran from one who received it, and Affan said: from one who receives it, from Jibril, peace be upon him, while it is fresh."
"21430","Abdullah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us: Bishr ibn Umar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Ali ibn Zayd from Yusuf al-Makki from Ibn Abbas from Ubayy who said: The last verse sent down: There has certainly come to you a Messenger from among yourselves, the verse."
"21431","Abu Uthman Amr ibn Muhammad ibn Bukayr al-Naqid narrated to me: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us from Amr, meaning Ibn Dinar, from Saeed ibn Jubayr who said: I said to Ibn Abbas: Nawf al-Shami claims, or says: Musa the companion of Khadir is not Musa of Bani Israil. He said: Nawf, enemy of Allah, lied. Ubayy ibn Kab narrated to me from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that Musa, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, stood among Bani Israil as a preacher, so they said to him: Who is the most knowledgeable of people. He said: I. So Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed to him that I have a servant more knowledgeable than you. He said: My Lord, show him to me. He said: It was said: Take a fish and place it in a basket, and wherever you lose it, he is there. He said: So he took a fish and placed it in a basket, and he and his companion walked upon the shore until they came to the rock. Musa, peace be upon him, slept, and the fish stirred in the basket and fell into the sea, so Allah held back the flow of water over it and the water stirred, then Musa awoke and said to his youth: Bring us our morning meal, we have indeed met from this journey of ours fatigue, and fatigue did not afflict him until he passed what Allah, Blessed and Exalted, commanded him of. He said: So he said: Did you see when we retreated to the rock, I forgot the fish, and none made me forget it except Satan. So they returned upon their tracks retracing, and began tracing their traces, and it took its way into the sea as a tunnel. He said: He held back the flow of water from it, so it became over it like an arch, so it was for the fish a tunnel and for Musa, peace be upon him, a wonder, until they ended at the rock, and there was a man wrapped in a garment, so Musa greeted him, and he said: And how is greeting in your land. He said: I am Musa. He said: Musa of Bani Israil. He said: Yes. May I follow you upon that you teach me of what you were taught right guidance. He said: O Musa, I am upon knowledge from Allah, Blessed and Exalted, you do not know it, and you are upon knowledge from Allah which Allah taught you. So they set out walking upon the shore, and a ship passed, and they recognized al-Khadir, so he was carried without fare, and it did not please him, and he looked at the ship and took the adze intending to break a plank from it, so he said: We were carried without fare and you want to breach it to drown its people. He said: Did I not say you will never be able to have patience with me. He said: I forgot. And a sparrow came and pecked in the sea. Al-Khadir said: My knowledge and your knowledge do not diminish from the knowledge of Allah, Exalted, except as this sparrow diminishes from this sea. So they set out until they came to people of a village, they asked its people for food and they refused to host them, then he saw a boy and took his head and pulled it off, so he said: Have you killed a pure soul without a soul, you have certainly come to a heinous thing. He said: Did I not say to you you will never be able to have patience with me. Sufyan said: Amr said: And this is severer than the first. He said: So they set out, and there was a wall wanting to collapse, so he erected it, and Sufyan showed us with his hands, raising his hands thus as a raising, placing his palms and raising them with the insides of his hands as a raising, and he said: If you wished you could have taken wage for it. He said: This is parting between me and you. Ibn Abbas said: The first was forgetfulness. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy upon Musa, had he been patient until He narrated to us of his affair."
"21432","Amr al-Naqid narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us from Amr from Saeed ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas from Ubayy ibn Kab from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: If you wished you could have taken wage for it."
"21433","Amr al-Naqid narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us from Amr from Saeed ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas from Ubayy ibn Kab from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): And there was a wall wanting to collapse, so he erected it. He said: With his hand, and he raised them both as a raising."
"21434","Bahz ibn Asad narrated to us: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to me as dictation upon me from Amr from Saeed ibn Jubayr who said: I said to Ibn Abbas, my father said: I wrote it from Bahz and Ibn Uyaynah, that Nawf claims that Musa is not the companion of al-Khadir. So he said: Enemy of Allah lied. Ubayy ibn Kab narrated to us from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Musa, peace be upon him, stood as a preacher among Bani Israil, and was asked which people is most knowledgeable. He said: I. So Allah blamed him since he did not return knowledge to Him. He said: Rather, a servant of Mine at the junction of the two seas is more knowledgeable than you. He said: O my Lord, how for me to him. He said: Take a fish and place it in a basket, then set out, and wherever you lose it, he is there. So Musa set out, with him his youth, walking, until they ended at the rock. Musa, peace be upon him, slept, and the fish stirred in the basket and went out and fell into the sea, so Allah held back the flow of water like an arch, and it was for the fish a tunnel. Sufyan said: So he joined the thumb and forefinger and parted between them. He said: So they set out until when it was next day Musa said to his youth: Bring us our morning meal, we have indeed met from this journey of ours fatigue. He said: And he did not find fatigue until he passed where he was commanded. He said: That is what we were seeking. So they returned upon their tracks retracing, tracing their traces. He said: And the trace of the fish was for Musa a wonder, and for the fish a tunnel, and he mentioned the hadith."
"21435","Abu Bakr Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us from Israil from Abu Ishaq from Saeed ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: We were with him, and the people said: Nawf al-Shami claims that he who went seeking knowledge is not Musa of Bani Israil, and Ibn Abbas was reclining, so he sat upright and said: Likewise, O Saeed. I said: Yes, I heard him say that. So Ibn Abbas said: Nawf lied. Ubayy ibn Kab narrated to me that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Mercy of Allah upon us and upon Salih, mercy of Allah upon us and upon the brother of Ad. Then he said: Musa, peace be upon him, while he was preaching his people one day, said to them: There is not upon earth anyone more knowledgeable than me. And Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed to him that upon earth is one more knowledgeable than you, and the sign of that is that you take provision of a salted fish, and when you lose it, he is where you lose it. So he took provision of a salted fish and set out, he and his youth, until when they reached the place they were commanded, when they ended at the rock, Musa went to seek and his youth placed the fish upon the rock, and it stirred and took its way into the sea as a tunnel. His youth said: When the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) comes I shall tell him, but Satan made him forget. So they set out, and there befell them what befalls the traveler of fatigue and weariness, and there did not befall him what befalls the traveler of fatigue and weariness until he passed what he was commanded. So Musa said to his youth: Bring us our morning meal, we have indeed met from this journey of ours fatigue. His youth said to him: O Prophet of Allah, did you see when we retreated to the rock, I forgot to tell you, and none made me forget it except Satan, and it took its way into the sea as a tunnel. He said: That is what we were seeking. So they returned upon their tracks retracing, tracing the trace, until when they ended at the rock he circled it, and there he was wrapped in a garment of his, so he greeted him, and he raised his head and said to him: Who are you. He said: Musa. He said: Which Musa. He said: Musa of Bani Israil. He said: I was told you have knowledge, so I wanted to accompany you. He said: You will never be able to have patience with me. He said: You shall find me, if Allah wills, patient, and I shall not disobey you a command. He said: How shall you be patient upon what you have not encompassed in awareness. He said: I was commanded to do it. He said: You shall find me, if Allah wills, patient. He said: If you follow me, do not ask me about anything until I make mention of it to you. So they set out until when they boarded in the ship, those in it went out and he stayed behind to breach it. Musa said to him: You breach it to drown its people, you have certainly come to a dreadful thing. He said: Did I not say you will never be able to have patience with me. He said: Take me not for what I forgot, and burden me not in my affair with hardship. So they set out until when they came upon boys playing upon the seashore, and among them a boy, no boy among the boys cleaner, meaning than him, so he took him and killed him. Musa, peace be upon him, recoiled at that and said: Have you killed a pure soul without a soul, you have certainly come to a heinous thing. He said: Did I not say to you you will never be able to have patience with me. He said: Shame from his companion seized him and he was embarrassed, so he said: If I ask you about anything after it, do not keep me company, you have reached from me an excuse. So they set out until when they came to people of a mean village, they asked its people for food, and Musa, peace be upon him, was afflicted with hunger, but they did not host them, then they found therein a wall wanting to collapse, so he erected it. Musa said to him, from what befell them of hunger: If you wished you could have taken wage for it. He said: This is parting between me and you. So Musa, peace be upon him, took the edge of his garment and said: Tell me. So he said: As for the ship, it belonged to poor people working in the sea, and behind them was a king taking every ship by force, so when he passed over it and saw it breached he left it, and its people patched it with a piece of wood and benefited by it. And as for the boy, he was stamped the day he was stamped a disbeliever, and love for him was cast upon his parents, and had they obeyed him he would have burdened them with transgression and disbelief, so we wanted their Lord to replace for them better than him in purity and nearer in affection, and his father fell upon his mother and she conceived and bore from him better than him in purity and nearer in affection. And as for the wall, it belonged to two orphan boys in the city, and beneath it was a treasure for them, and their father was righteous, so your Lord willed they reach their maturity and extract their treasure as mercy from your Lord, and I did it not upon my order. That is the interpretation of what you could not have patience upon."
"21436","Abdullah ibn Ibrahim al-Marwazi narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn Yusuf narrated to me in the tafsir of Ibn Jurayj which he dictated to them: Yala ibn Muslim and Amr ibn Dinar informed me from Saeed ibn Jubayr, one adding over the other, and others said: I heard him narrating it from Saeed ibn Jubayr who said: We were with Abdullah ibn Abbas in his house when he said: Ask me. So I said: Abu Abbas, may Allah make me ransom for you, in Kufah a storyteller called Nawf claims he is not Musa of Bani Israil. As for Amr ibn Dinar, he said: Enemy of Allah lied. And as for Yala ibn Muslim, he said: Ibn Abbas said: Ubayy ibn Kab narrated to me, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Musa, the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, reminded people one day until eyes overflowed and hearts softened, then he turned, and a man caught him and said: O Messenger of Allah, is there upon earth anyone more knowledgeable than you. He said: No. He said: So he was blamed since he did not return knowledge to Allah, Blessed and Exalted. So Allah revealed to him: I have a servant more knowledgeable than you. He said: O my Lord, and how. He said: The junction of the two seas. He said: O my Lord, make for me a sign I know that by. Amr said to me: He said: Where the fish leaves you. And Yala said: Take a dead fish, where breath is breathed into it. So he took a fish and placed it in a basket. He said to his youth: I charge you only to tell me where the fish leaves you. He said: You did not charge me much. That is His saying, Blessed and Exalted: When Musa said to his youth Yusha ibn Nun, it is not from Saeed ibn Jubayr. He said: While he was in the shade of a rock in a moist place, the fish flapped, while Musa was sleeping. His youth said: I shall not wake him, until when he awoke he forgot to tell him. And the fish flapped until it entered the sea, so Allah, Blessed and Exalted, held back the flow of the sea over it until its trace was as if in stone. Amr said to me: As if its trace in stone. And he circled his thumbs and those next to them. We have indeed met from this journey of ours fatigue. He said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, cut off fatigue from you, it is not this from Saeed ibn Jubayr. So he told him, and they returned and found Khadir, peace be upon him. Uthman ibn Abi Sulayman said to me: Upon a green carpet upon the liver of the sea. Saeed ibn Jubayr said: His garment wrapped, he placed its edge beneath his feet and its edge beneath his head. So Musa greeted him, and he uncovered his face and said: Is there in your land greeting, who are you. He said: I am Musa. He said: Musa of Bani Israil. He said: Yes. He said: What is your affair. He said: I came that you teach me of what you were taught right guidance. He said: Does it not suffice you that the tidings of the Torah are in your hand and revelation comes to you, O Musa, I have knowledge it is not proper you know it, and you have knowledge it is not proper I know it. So a bird came and took with its beak. He said: By Allah, my knowledge and your knowledge in the knowledge of Allah are only as this bird took with its beak from the sea. Until when they boarded in the ship, they found small ferries carrying people of this shore to this shore, they knew him and said: The righteous servant of Allah. So we said to Saeed: Khadir. He said: Yes. They do not carry him for wage. So he breached it and drove a peg in it. Musa said: Have you breached it to drown its people, you have certainly come to a dreadful thing. He said: Mujahid said: Heinous. He said: Did I not say you will never be able to have patience with me, and the first was forgetfulness, the second a condition, and the third deliberate. He said: Take me not for what I forgot, and burden me not in my affair with hardship. So they met a boy and he killed him. Yala ibn Muslim said: Saeed ibn Jubayr said: They found boys playing, so he took a disbelieving boy, he was handsome, and laid him down then slaughtered him with the knife. He said: Have you killed a pure soul that did not act with sin. So they set out and found a wall wanting to collapse, so he erected it. Saeed said: With his hand thus, and raised his hand and it stood straight. Yala said: I thought Saeed said: So he wiped it with his hand and it stood straight. He said: If you wished you could have taken wage for it. Saeed said: Wage we eat. He said: And he used to recite it: And before them. And Ibn Abbas used to recite it: And before them a king, they claim from other than Saeed that he said: This killed boy, they claim his name is Jaysur. He said: Taking every ship by force, and he wanted when it passed him to leave it for its defect, and when they passed they repaired it and benefited by it afterwards, some of them say: They plugged it with a bottle, and some say: With tar. And his parents were believers and he was a disbeliever, so we feared he would burden them with transgression and disbelief, and his love would carry them to follow him upon his religion, so we wanted their Lord to replace for them better than him in purity and nearer in affection, they are more merciful to him than them to the first whom Khadir killed. And others than Saeed claimed they both said: A girl. And as for Dawud ibn Abi Asim, he said from more than one: It is a girl. And it reached me from Saeed ibn Jubayr that it is a girl. And I found it in my father's book from Yahya ibn Main from Hisham ibn Yusuf similar to it."
"21437","And I found it in my father's book from Yahya ibn Main from Hisham ibn Yusuf similar to it."
"21438","Muhammad ibn Yaqub Abu al-Haytham al-Zubbali narrated to me, saying: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: I heard my father: Raqabah narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Saeed ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas: Ubayy ibn Kab narrated to us, saying: I heard the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: While Musa, peace be upon him, among his people reminding them of the days of Allah, and the days of Allah are His blessings and His trials, said: I know not upon earth a man better than me or more knowledgeable than me. He said: So Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed to him: I know better of good who he is, or with whom it is: Upon earth is a man more knowledgeable than you. He said: O my Lord, guide me to him. So it was said to him: Take provision of a salted fish. So he did, then went out and met al-Khadir, and of their affair was what was, until the last of that they passed by the mean village, its people mean, and they went about in the assemblies and asked for food, but they refused to host them. Then he narrated to him the tidings, the tidings of the ship, that he only breached it that the king pass it by and not want it. And as for the boy, he was stamped the day he was stamped a disbeliever, his parents pitied him, and had he reached maturity he would have burdened them with transgression and disbelief. And as for the wall, it belonged to two orphan boys in the city."
"21439","Abu al-Rabi al-Ataki Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Zahrani narrated to us: al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: I heard my father mentioning from Raqabah. And Abdullah narrated to us, saying: And Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to me: Mutamir narrated to us from his father from Raqabah. And Abdullah narrated to us, saying: And Suwayd ibn Saeed narrated to me. And Abdullah narrated to us, saying: And Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Wasiti narrated to me, both saying: Mutamir narrated to us from his father from Raqabah, and they all said: From Abu Ishaq from Saeed ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas from Ubayy ibn Kab from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The boy whom al-Khadir killed was stamped a disbeliever. Abu al-Rabi added in his hadith: Had he reached maturity he would have burdened his parents with transgression and disbelief."
"21440","Surayj ibn Yunus and Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, both saying: Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us: Abd al-Jabbar ibn Abbas al-Hamdani narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Saeed ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas from Ubayy ibn Kab from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The boy whom the companion of Musa, peace be upon him, killed was stamped the day he was stamped a disbeliever."
"21441","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us: Abu Dawud Umar ibn Sad narrated to us from Yahya ibn Zakariya ibn Abi Zaidah from Hamzah from Abu Ishaq from Saeed ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas from Ubayy that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: If I ask you about anything after it, do not keep me company, you have reached from me an excuse."
"21442","Abu Abdullah al-Anbari narrated to us: Umayyah ibn Khalid narrated to us: Abu al-Jariyah al-Abdi narrated to us from Shubah from Abu Ishaq from Saeed ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas from Ubayy ibn Kab from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he recited: You have reached from me an excuse, giving it weight."
"21443","Abdullah narrated to us: Hajjaj ibn Yusuf al-Shair narrated to us, saying: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to me, I asked him: my father narrated to us, saying: I heard Ayyub narrating from Saeed ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas from Ubayy ibn Kab that Jibril, when he struck Zamzam with his heel, Umm Ismail began gathering the gravel, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy upon Hajar, Umm Ismail, had she left it, it would have been flowing water."
"21444","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us: Hamzah ibn Habib al-Zayyat narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Saeed ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas from Ubayy ibn Kab who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he supplicated for anyone began with himself, so he mentioned Musa one day and said: Mercy of Allah upon us and upon Musa, had he been patient Allah, Exalted, would have narrated to us of his tidings, but he said: If I ask you about anything after it, do not keep me company, you have reached from me an excuse."
"21445","Hajjaj and Abu Qatan Amr ibn al-Haytham narrated to us, both saying: Hamzah narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Saeed ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas from Ubayy ibn Kab from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) its meaning."
"21446","Abdullah narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abdullah, freedman of Bani Hashim, narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Aban al-Jafi narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Saeed ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas from Ubayy ibn Kab from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning His saying, Blessed and Exalted: And remind them of the days of Allah. He said: By the blessings of Allah, Blessed and Exalted."
"21447","Abdullah narrated to us: Abu Abdullah al-Anbari narrated to us: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Saeed ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas from Ubayy similar to it, and he did not raise it."
"21448","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim Abu Yahya al-Bazzaz narrated to me: Abu al-Walid Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, saying: Qays narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Saeed ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas from Ubayy that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he mentioned the prophets began with himself, and said: Mercy of Allah upon us and upon Hud and upon Salih."
"21449","Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Maymun al-Qaddah narrated to us: Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Sadiq narrated to us from Ibn Shihab from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah from Ibn Abbas who said: A man from Bani Fazarah disputed with me concerning the man whom Musa, peace be upon him, followed, so I said: He is al-Khadir, peace be upon him, and the Fazari said: He is another man. Then Ubayy ibn Kab passed by us. Ibn Abbas said: So I called him and asked him: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mention he whom Musa, peace be upon him, followed. He said: Yes, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: While Musa was sitting among a company of Bani Israil, a man said to him: Is anyone more knowledgeable of Allah, Blessed and Exalted, than you. He said: I do not deem so. So Allah revealed to him: Yes, My servant al-Khadir. So he asked the way to him, and Allah, Blessed and Exalted, made the fish a sign for him, if he missed it, and of his affair was what Allah, Blessed and Exalted, narrated."
